<title>BRAZIL: Brazil two coffee exporter groups to meet May 5.</title>
<headline>Brazil two coffee exporter groups to meet May 5.</headline>
<dateline>RIO DE JANEIRO 1997-04-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazil's two coffee exporter entities are to meet on May 5 to discuss the possibility of a new united organisation, said a spokesman for the Brazilian Coffee Exporters' Federation (Febec).</p>
<p>A six-man commission -- three members each from Febec and the Association of Brazilian Coffee Exporters (Abecafe) -- will hold their first talks in Santos, he added.</p>
<p>Febec is Brazil's traditional exporter association, but in November 1995 a group of exporters formed Abecafe in protest at a plan to divide out coffee export quotas internally.</p>
<p>Febec elections for all officers were due to be held at the end of this month but will now be held at the end of May to allow time for the negotiations between the two groups, the Febec spokesman said.</p>
<p>((--Caroline Bulloch, Rio de Janeiro newsroom +55 21 507 4151))</p>
